[32m+[m[32m<p>This exponent calculator evaluates expressions of the form <strong>xⁿ</strong> and <strong>ⁿ√x</strong> for any real numbers. It supports positive exponents, negative exponents (which produce reciprocals), fractional exponents (which produce roots), and zero exponents. The calculator also handles square roots (√), cube roots (³√), and arbitrary nth roots, making it a complete tool for all exponentiation and root operations.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m<h2>How Exponents Work</h2>[m
[32m+[m[32m<p>Exponentiation is repeated multiplication: <strong>xⁿ</strong> means x multiplied by itself n times. For example, 2³ = 2 × 2 × 2 = 8. But exponents can be more than just whole numbers:</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m<ul>[m
[32m+[m[32m  <li><strong>Positive exponent:</strong> xⁿ means x multiplied by itself n times. Example: 5³ = 125</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m  <li><strong>Negative exponent:</strong> x⁻ⁿ = 1/xⁿ. Example: 2⁻³ = 1/8 = 0.125</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m  <li><strong>Zero exponent:</strong> x⁰ = 1 (for any x ≠ 0). Example: 7⁰ = 1</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m  <li><strong>Fractional exponent:</strong> x^(1/n) = ⁿ√x. Example: 27^(1/3) = ³√27 = 3</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m  <li><strong>General fractional exponent:</strong> x^(m/n) = (ⁿ√x)ᵐ = ⁿ√(xᵐ). Example: 8^(2/3) = (³√8)² = 2² = 4</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m</ul>[m
[32m+[m
